cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, the released weights, or the frozen evaluation folds, please cite the paper."
title: "GlucoPRISM: reserved subspaces for CGM foundation models"
abstract: >-
  Code, weights and reproduction scripts for "Naming the Nuisance: Reserved
  Subspaces Buy Control, Not Disentanglement, in CGM Foundation Models".
  Includes two released models, reproductions of four CGM foundation models on
  a public-only corpus, seven zero-shot time-series baselines under a single
  probe, and the frozen evaluation folds used for every reported number.
authors:
  - name: "The GlucoPRISM authors"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - continuous glucose monitoring
  - foundation models
  - representation learning
  - shortcut learning
  - concept erasure
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: "Naming the Nuisance: Reserved Subspaces Buy Control, Not Disentanglement, in CGM Foundation Models"
  authors:
    - name: "The GlucoPRISM authors"
  year: 2026
